SSA transport and unchanged kernel reductions — 2026-10-16

Scope: ordinary Rust translation validation, then forwarding across asm-goto
edges without fixed register bindings. No new Lean profile or kernel acceptance.
The checker compares actual SSA and post-SSA programs. It does not rerun the
producer. The independent allocation relation still checks the next boundary.

The initial three mutations changed a retained input, operation or return.
All three passed the old post-SSA-only allocation boundary and now fail the
transport check. Additional cases cover demand, entry identity, classes,
loops, copy cycles, critical edges, effects, and asm-goto outputs and attributes.
With the check alone, both original reduction assembly files were byte-identical.

